# Mobile Forms Design System

This document outlines the standardized mobile form patterns and components used throughout the BetterPack application.

## Design Philosophy

BetterPack follows a mobile-first approach with consistent, accessible form experiences across all devices:

- **Mobile**: Forms slide up from bottom of screen as drawers
- **Desktop**: Forms appear as centered modals
- **Consistent**: Same components, styling, and behavior everywhere
- **Accessible**: Proper focus management, touch targets, keyboard navigation

## Core Components

### MobileFormDrawer

The foundational component for all form presentations in the app.

```tsx
import { MobileFormDrawer } from '@/components/ui/mobile-form-drawer'

<MobileFormDrawer
  isOpen={showForm}
  onClose={() => setShowForm(false)}
  title="Form Title"
  primaryAction={{
    label: 'Save',
    onClick: handleSave,
    loading: saving
  }}
  secondaryAction={{
    label: 'Cancel',
    onClick: handleCancel
  }}
>
  <div className="p-6">
    {/* Form content */}
  </div>
</MobileFormDrawer>
```

**Key Features:**
- Auto-slides from bottom on mobile, centers on desktop
- Focus management (auto-focus first input, trap focus, restore on close)
- Keyboard shortcuts (Escape to close)
- Backdrop click to close
- Loading states for async actions
- Consistent header with title and close button
- Sticky footer with action buttons

### Custom Select Component

Replaces native HTML `<select>` elements for better mobile experience.

```tsx
import { SimpleSelect } from '@/components/ui/select'

// Simple string options
<SimpleSelect
  value={selectedValue}
  onChange={setValue}
  options={['Option 1', 'Option 2', 'Option 3']}
  placeholder="Choose option..."
/>

// Complex options with custom labels
<Select
  value={selectedValue}
  onChange={setValue}
  options={[
    { value: 'val1', label: 'Custom Label 1' },
    { value: 'val2', label: 'Custom Label 2' }
  ]}
/>
```

**Key Features:**
- Proper mobile positioning (no viewport issues)
- Touch-friendly 44px minimum height
- Keyboard navigation (arrow keys, Enter, Escape)
- Visual selection indicators
- Consistent styling with other form elements

## Implementation Patterns

### Form Wrapper Pattern

Each form should have two components:

1. **Form Component** - Pure form logic and fields
2. **Form Wrapper** - Handles presentation with MobileFormDrawer

```tsx
// AddGearForm.tsx - Pure form logic
export function AddGearForm({ onAdd, onCancel, standalone = true }) {
  // Form logic here

  return (
    <form data-add-gear-form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
      {/* Form fields */}
    </form>
  )
}

// AddGearFormWrapper.tsx - Presentation wrapper
export function AddGearFormWrapper({ isOpen, onAdd, onCancel }) {
  return (
    <MobileFormDrawer
      isOpen={isOpen}
      onClose={onCancel}
      title="Add Gear"
      primaryAction={{
        label: 'Add Gear',
        onClick: () => {
          // Trigger form submission
          document.querySelector('[data-add-gear-form]')?.requestSubmit()
        }
      }}
    >
      <div className="p-6">
        <AddGearForm onAdd={onAdd} onCancel={onCancel} standalone={false} />
      </div>
    </MobileFormDrawer>
  )
}
```

### Form Field Standards

All form fields must follow these standards:

```tsx
// Minimum touch target size
className="min-h-[44px]"

// Proper labeling
<Label htmlFor="field-id">Field Name</Label>
<Input id="field-id" ... />

// Error states
<Input className={error ? 'border-red-500' : ''} />
{error && <p className="text-red-500 text-sm">{error}</p>}

// Required field indicators
<Label>Field Name <span className="text-red-500">*</span></Label>

// Mobile-friendly input types
inputMode="decimal" // for number inputs
inputMode="numeric" // for integer inputs
```

### Layout Patterns

```tsx
// Two-column responsive layout
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
  <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <Label>Field 1</Label>
    <Input />
  </div>
  <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <Label>Field 2</Label>
    <Input />
  </div>
</div>

// Single column layout
<div className="space-y-4">
  <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <Label>Field</Label>
    <Input />
  </div>
</div>

// Inline inputs with labels
<div className="flex gap-2">
  <Input className="flex-1" />
  <SimpleSelect className="min-w-[70px]" />
</div>
```

## Accessibility Requirements

### Focus Management
- Auto-focus first input when form opens (300ms delay for animation)
- Tab order follows logical flow
- Focus returns to trigger element when form closes
- Focus trapped within modal during interaction

### Keyboard Navigation
- **Escape**: Close form
- **Enter**: Submit form (when appropriate)
- **Arrow keys**: Navigate select options
- **Tab/Shift+Tab**: Move between fields

### Touch Targets
- Minimum 44x44px for all interactive elements
- Adequate spacing between touch targets (8px minimum)
- Visual feedback for touch interactions

### Screen Reader Support
- Proper semantic HTML structure
- ARIA labels and descriptions where needed
- Form validation messages announced
- Modal dialog roles and properties

## CSS Classes and Animations

### Mobile Drawer Animations
```css
.mobile-form-drawer {
  /* Mobile: slide up from bottom */
  animation: slideUpMobile 0.3s ease-out;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .mobile-form-drawer {
    /* Desktop: scale up from center */
    animation: scaleUp 0.2s ease-out;
  }
}
```

### Standard Form Classes
```css
/* Form containers */
.form-container { padding: 1.5rem; }
.form-section { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
.form-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }

/* Mobile-specific */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .form-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .touch-target { min-height: 44px; }
}
```

## Testing Guidelines

### Manual Testing Checklist

#### Mobile (iOS Safari, Android Chrome)
- [ ] Form slides up smoothly from bottom
- [ ] First input auto-focuses after animation
- [ ] Touch targets are adequate size (44px+)
- [ ] Select dropdowns position correctly
- [ ] Form scrolls properly when keyboard appears
- [ ] Backdrop tap closes form
- [ ] Swipe gestures work as expected

#### Desktop (Chrome, Firefox, Safari)
- [ ] Form centers as modal
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works
- [ ] Focus management is correct
- [ ] Resize handling works properly
- [ ] Click outside closes form

#### Accessibility
- [ ] Screen reader announces form opening/closing
- [ ] All fields properly labeled
- [ ] Error messages announced
- [ ] Focus order is logical
- [ ] Keyboard-only navigation possible

### Automated Testing

```tsx
// Example form test
describe('AddGearFormWrapper', () => {
  it('should show mobile drawer when open', () => {
    render(<AddGearFormWrapper isOpen={true} onAdd={jest.fn()} onCancel={jest.fn()} />)
    expect(screen.getByRole('dialog')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(screen.getByText('Add Gear')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })

  it('should focus first input after animation', async () => {
    render(<AddGearFormWrapper isOpen={true} onAdd={jest.fn()} onCancel={jest.fn()} />)
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(screen.getByLabelText(/name/i)).toHaveFocus()
    }, { timeout: 500 })
  })

  it('should submit form when primary action clicked', async () => {
    const onAdd = jest.fn()
    render(<AddGearFormWrapper isOpen={true} onAdd={onAdd} onCancel={jest.fn()} />)

    // Fill form
    fireEvent.change(screen.getByLabelText(/name/i), { target: { value: 'Test Item' } })
    fireEvent.change(screen.getByLabelText(/weight/i), { target: { value: '100' } })

    // Click primary action
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Add Gear'))

    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(onAdd).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.objectContaining({
        name: 'Test Item',
        weight_grams: 100
      }))
    })
  })
})
```

## Common Issues and Solutions

### Issue: Form fields too small on mobile
**Solution**: Use `min-h-[44px]` class on all interactive elements

### Issue: Select dropdowns cut off on mobile
**Solution**: Use custom `SimpleSelect` component instead of native `<select>`

### Issue: Form submission not working with drawer buttons
**Solution**: Use `form.requestSubmit()` in drawer button onClick, ensure form has `data-` attribute

### Issue: Focus not restored after form closes
**Solution**: Store reference to trigger element and restore focus in useEffect cleanup

### Issue: Keyboard covers form fields on mobile
**Solution**: Use `max-h-[90vh]` on drawer and ensure content is scrollable

## Migration Guide

To migrate existing forms to the new pattern:

1. **Wrap form with MobileFormDrawer**:
   ```tsx
   // Before
   <div className="modal">
     <MyForm />
   </div>

   // After
   <MobileFormDrawer isOpen={showForm} onClose={closeForm}>
     <div className="p-6">
       <MyForm standalone={false} />
     </div>
   </MobileFormDrawer>
   ```

2. **Replace native selects**:
   ```tsx
   // Before
   <select value={value} onChange={e => setValue(e.target.value)}>
     <option value="a">A</option>
   </select>

   // After
   <SimpleSelect
     value={value}
     onChange={setValue}
     options={['A', 'B', 'C']}
   />
   ```

3. **Update touch targets**:
   ```tsx
   // Add to all interactive elements
   className="min-h-[44px]"
   ```

4. **Add proper form attributes**:
   ```tsx
   <form data-my-form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
   ```

This standardized approach ensures consistent, accessible, and mobile-friendly forms throughout the BetterPack application.

